diff --git a/docs/cli.rst b/docs/cli.rst
index a096fdeaa7887dacb1a4d37aa15f76c4236763e6..1dc717e2409dcb44184ab452863daaf41a3bcac7 100644
--- a/docs/cli.rst
+++ b/docs/cli.rst
@@ -712,6 +712,16 @@ You can delete all the existing rows in the table before inserting the new recor
 
     $ sqlite-utils insert dogs.db dogs dogs.json --truncate
 
+You can transform each incoming JSON object using the ``--convert`` option.
+The Python code is evaluated against each object as ``row`` before it is
+inserted. For example, this converts ``n`` to an integer and increments it::
+
+    $ sqlite-utils insert data.db numbers numbers.json \
+        --convert 'row["n"] = int(row["n"]) + 1'
+
+Every incoming object is preserved; the conversion code mutates each ``row``
+in place.
+
 .. _cli_inserting_data_binary:
 
 Inserting binary data
